# Teleportation Simulation Pipeline (TP-001 to TP-006)
[cite_start]**Aura Research Project Architecture** **Inventor:** Seriki Yakub (KUBU LEE) [cite: 245]  
[cite_start]**Core Framework:** Intelligent Spreadsheet Language Core (`.xlsl`) [cite: 245]

---

## Pipeline Overview
[cite_start]This notebook executes the multi-stage teleportation simulation pipeline, evaluating quantum fidelity, spatial transformation stability, and logical boundary conditions across six scale thresholds[cite: 246, 754]:

1. [cite_start]**TP-001: Photon** (Feasible) 
2. [cite_start]**TP-002: Electron** (Experimental) 
3. [cite_start]**TP-003: C60 Molecule** (Mesoscopic) 
4. [cite_start]**TP-004: Virus** (Biological Edge) 
5. [cite_start]**TP-005: Neuron Cluster** (Cognitive Link) 
6. [cite_start]**TP-006: Human** (Infeasible / Boundary Restricted) 

[cite_start]The pipeline integrates parameters from `.xquant` (quantum states), `.xdim` (dimensional vectors), `.xphilo` (deontic logic bounds), and `.xsim` (environmental stressors), streaming live telemetry into `.xlog`[cite: 246, 508, 510, 512, 515, 812, 813].
